// The tsconfig the PUBLISHED build reads, and the only thing it changes is what
// is in scope: `src/__tests__` is out.
//
// `tsconfig.json` deliberately keeps it in, because `tsc --noEmit` has to check
// it. The declaration build has the opposite requirement — a `.d.ts` emitted
// for a test lands in the consumer's `node_modules` and references `jest` and
// `@testing-library/react-native`, which a consumer has no reason to have
// installed. The babel targets already skip the directory; only `tsc` reads a
// tsconfig, so only `tsc` needed telling.
//
// The colocated `src/compiler/inheritance.test.ts` is deliberately NOT excluded.
// Its declaration is part of the published 3.0.7 package, and dropping it here
// would be a second, unrelated change wearing this one's clothes.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "src/__tests__"]
}
